<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Universal Declaration of Human Rights</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Universal Declaration of Human Rights is a statement of fundamental rights and freedoms adopted by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-general-assembly">United Nations General Assembly</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> on 10 December 1948. Drafted by a commission chaired by Eleanor Roosevelt, from a first draft by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-peters-humphrey">John Peters Humphrey</a>, its thirty articles set out civil, political, economic and social rights and became the foundation of international human rights law.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/universal-declaration-of-human-rights.jpg" alt="Universal Declaration of Human Rights" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FDR Presidential Library &amp;amp; Museum · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eleanor_Roosevelt_UDHR.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
